  { title: 'Your content stays on your servers.', text: `Cloudflare keeps no copy or catalog of your pages. A crawler gets the list of domains that charge it and finds the pages itself (${a(C.discover, 'Discover payable content')}). "The Cloudflare CDN does not cache HTML or JSON by default", so each crawl normally reaches your origin (${a(C.cache, 'Default cache behavior')}).` },
  { title: 'Cloudflare decides which bots you can charge.', text: `You choose Charge, Allow or Block only for crawlers on Cloudflare's list. Bot operators apply to join it, and "Cloudflare reserves the right to re-assign Verified bot categories" (${a(C.verifiedBots, 'Verified bots')}). A bot it doesn't list can't be charged. On the free plan, AI Crawl Control "identifies AI crawlers based on their user agent strings" (${a(C.manage, 'Manage AI crawlers')}).` },
  { title: 'Your other rules run first.', text: `Firewall rules and bot tools act before Pay Per Crawl, so a crawler they block is never offered a price (${a(C.waf, 'AI Crawl Control with WAF')}).` },
  { title: 'Per-page prices need a header.', text: `Since June 2026, your origin or a Worker can price each page in a response header (${a(C.advanced, 'Advanced configuration')}).` },
  { title: 'Refusals and redirects.', text: `A blocked crawler gets a 403 (refused), or on paid plans a 402 (pay first) with a message of your own (${a(C.manage, 'Manage AI crawlers')}). The one redirect shipped sends a verified AI crawler to the page's canonical URL (${a(C.redirects, 'Redirects for AI Training')}), not to a license or a marketplace.` },
  { title: 'Logs.', text: `Cloudflare's log export, Logpush, streams each request with a Pay Per Crawl outcome, whose values aren't listed (${a(C.logpush, 'Logpush')}).` },
  { title: 'FORA agents and Cloudflare\'s signature check.', text: `Cloudflare's verifier reads an older form of Web Bot Auth than the one FORA's software sends, and "will fail to verify a message if" it uses the later form (${a(C.webBotAuth, 'Web Bot Auth')}). So Cloudflare can't verify a FORA agent by its signature, and the agent can't pay Pay Per Crawl with it. FORA sales don't depend on it: the agent brings a signed link, which FORA's Worker checks. Let signed requests through your rules, as under Running both. The working group's -01, of 2026-10-29, lets a verifier accept Cloudflare's older form and tells signers to send the form FORA's software sends (${a(C.draft01, 'draft-ietf-webbotauth-httpsig-protocol-01')}).` },
];

