<LandingLayout
  title="Cloudflare and FORA — FORA resources"
  description="How Cloudflare charges AI crawlers on its network, what that takes on your site, where it is ahead of FORA, and how a publisher on Cloudflare can run both."
>
  <AudienceHero
    current="resources"
    badge={`Resources · ${a('/resources/content-marketplaces/', 'Content marketplaces')} · Cloudflare`}
    title="Cloudflare charges AI crawlers on its network. <em>With FORA, you sell a license per resource.</em>"
    sub="If your site runs through Cloudflare, Cloudflare can charge an AI crawler (a program that fetches pages in bulk) for each page it takes, and pay you. FORA lets you set terms and a price for each resource, sold through the Exchanges you choose. Each sale leaves a signed record of what was bought, and on what terms. Here is how the two compare, what each asks of your site, and how they fit on one site."
    updated={resourceUpdated(HREF)}
  >
    <a href="#ahead" class="btn btn-primary">Where Cloudflare is ahead</a>
    <a href="#together" class="btn btn-ghost">Run both</a>
  </AudienceHero>

  <Band tone="near" id="glance" label="At a glance" title="Cloudflare and FORA, side by side" lead="The facts a revenue team and an engineering lead act on.">
    <GlanceCard vendor="Cloudflare (Pay Per Crawl; Pay Per Use where it differs)" groups={GLANCE} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="The short answer" title="Two ways to be paid for AI access">
    <CardGrid items={SHORT_ANSWER} />
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.exchange} />
    <div class="steps-wrap"><SaleSteps variant="web" /></div>
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="How you're paid" title="From a crawler's request to your monthly payout" lead="In both programs, Cloudflare charges the buyer and pays you monthly. They differ in who sets the price.">
    <Split aside="1.35fr">
      <Figure
        src={`${IMG}/cf-2.png`}
        title="Two programs, two price setters."
        alt="In Pay Per Crawl (closed beta) you set one price for every crawler set to Charge, Cloudflare quotes it with HTTP 402, charges each successful fetch and pays you monthly. Pay Per Use (beta) reverses who sets the price: the AI company sets a price for a use it defines, you accept or decline, the buyer reports its own uses, and Cloudflare charges the buyer and pays you monthly."
      />
      <Fragment slot="aside">
        <p class="prose"><b>Pay Per Crawl</b>, in six steps:</p>
        <StepList items={PPC_STEPS} />
        <p class="prose" set:html={`<b>Pay Per Use</b> reverses who sets the price (${a(C.payPerUse, 'Pay Per Use')}, published 2026-09-30). An AI company "defines the use it will pay for and sets a price", such as returning an excerpt of your page to a customer. You accept offers in the dashboard, with "no origin change". "Usage is self-reported": the buyer reports its own uses, and Cloudflare charges the buyer and pays you monthly. Its reason for the program: "AI products fetch far more than they use".`} />
      </Fragment>
    </Split>
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" compact label="Cloudflare in three numbers">
    <KeyFacts items={KEY_FACTS} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="Who has been paid so far" title="No paying buyer named for Pay Per Crawl">
    <PullQuote
      quote="Pay per crawl is currently in closed beta."
      who="Cloudflare"
      source="What is Pay Per Crawl"
      href={C.whatIs}
    />
    <p class="prose" set:html={`Cloudflare names no AI company paying through Pay Per Crawl in any doc, post or press release checked on 2026-11-14. Press Gazette reported on 2026-08-17 that it "remains in closed beta testing" (${a(C.pressGazette, 'Press Gazette')}). The publishers Cloudflare listed in 2025 were named "in support", not as participants. Participant counts and payout totals are not published.`} />
    <p class="prose" set:html={`For Pay Per Use, Cloudflare says it is "running experiments" with Ceramic.ai and You.com (${a(C.smarter, 'Making AI search smarter')}, published 2026-07-01).`} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" id="setup" label="What it takes on your site" title="What your engineer sets up, and what can break" lead="Pay Per Crawl needs your traffic routed through Cloudflare. Your other Cloudflare rules decide which crawlers it ever sees, and only crawlers on Cloudflare's list can be charged. Your content stays on your servers. Each point links Cloudflare's developer documentation.">
    <Split aside="380px">
      <Callout kind="engineers" collapse="Show the eight points" points={SETUP} />
      <Figure
        slot="aside"
        src={`${IMG}/cf-1.png`}
        title="Your zone, in the order a crawler meets it."
        alt="A crawler meets your DNS and proxy first (a hostname left unproxied never meets Pay Per Crawl), then your firewall rules and bot tools (a crawler they block is never offered a price), then Pay Per Crawl, where you set each listed crawler to Charge, Allow or Block; HTML isn't cached by default, so each crawl normally reaches your origin. The crawler gets the page if allowed, a 403 (refused) or a 402 (pay first) with your own message if blocked, a 402 (pay first) with the price if it is charged without an agreement, and the page, charged, if it agreed."
      />
    </Split>
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" label="What can go wrong" title="In Cloudflare's own docs">
    <Callout kind="caution" points={CAUTIONS}>
      <PullQuote
        small
        quote="Your accrued earnings balance is not currently visible in the dashboard."
        who="Cloudflare"
        source="Monitor activity"
        href={C.monitor}
      />
    </Callout>
    <Callout kind="search" id="search-traffic" text={SEARCH_FORA.text} links={SEARCH_FORA.links}>
      <p set:html={`Pay Per Crawl charges only the crawlers you set to Charge. A firewall rule that allows search engines doesn't exempt them: "The search engine bots will then be charged" (${a(C.waf, 'AI Crawl Control with WAF')}). Setting a search crawler to Charge "may negatively impact your site's SEO performance" (${a(C.selectCrawlers, 'Select crawlers to charge')}).`} />
    </Callout>
  </Band>

  <Band id="ahead" label="Where Cloudflare is ahead" title="Where Cloudflare is ahead of FORA">
    <p class="prose"><b>In short:</b> Cloudflare can block a crawler that won't pay at the edge of any site it fronts, once the owner sets that crawler to Charge, and collects and pays out the money itself. FORA can do neither: its edge enforces only where it's installed, and money moves outside the protocol.</p>
    <PointList items={AHEAD_FIRST} />
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.edgeFunction} />
    <PointList items={AHEAD_REST} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="The differences" title="Eight questions a publisher asks of any licensing deal" lead="Cloudflare runs one company's exchange inside its network; FORA is a protocol for many Exchanges. The two compete as exchanges, and work together on bot detection and hosting. The price and money rows compare different things: one number per fetch against a menu of terms, and a company that moves money against a protocol that doesn't.">
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.broker} />
    <CompareTable vendor="Cloudflare (Pay Per Crawl; Pay Per Use where it differs)" rows={COMPARE} />
    <p class="note table-foot" set:html={`FORA pins Web Bot Auth -00; the working group published -01 on 2026-10-29 ${cite(39, 41)}.`} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" id="together" label="Running both" title="Both on one site today">
    <h3 class="sub-h">Works today <StatusTag status="live" /></h3>
    <PointList items={WORKS} />
    <h3 class="sub-h">Doesn't fit</h3>
    <p class="prose"><b>Settling a FORA sale through Pay Per Crawl.</b> Pay Per Crawl charges when a crawler fetches a page. As of 2026-11-15, its docs describe no way to bill an amount for a sale made elsewhere.</p>
    <p class="prose"><b>A Cloudflare price a FORA agent can verify.</b> As of 2026-11-15, Cloudflare's docs describe no signed price or receipt. The crawler gets a header that states the amount charged.</p>
  </Band>

  <Band label="What to do" title="If your site is on Cloudflare">
    <PointList numbered items={TODO} />
    <Callout kind="legal" points={LEGAL} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" id="about">
    <Callout kind="about" points={ABOUT_FORA} columns />
    <section class="sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-label">
      <h2 class="end-label" id="sources-label">Sources</h2>
      <p class="note">Sources are checked on the date of publication.</p>
      <SourceList groups={SOURCES} compact numbered />
    </section>
    <SeriesNav current={HREF} />
  </Band>

  <ClosingCta
    title="Set your own terms <em>for AI access</em>"
    text="FORA is an open protocol: you set terms and a price per resource, and the Exchange signs each offer."
  >
    <a href="/getting-started/what-is-fora/" class="btn btn-primary">What is FORA?</a>
    <a href="/protocol/licensing-terms/" class="btn btn-ghost">Licensing terms</a>
    <a href="/resources/content-marketplaces/" class="btn btn-ghost">All content marketplaces</a>
  </ClosingCta>
</LandingLayout>

